    "reason": "[ev-9350ba799f1a] is only a PR title in the CLI changelog. It names an \"External Artifact API\" (RFC-0012) and points to PR 5292, but it doesn't give the API group, version or kind, what changed, or the effect on existing environments. Nearby items show that a kind called `ExternalArtifact` exists: `flux trace` now supports it [ev-649350cce0ab], and source-watcher and `ArtifactGenerator` were added [ev-3ab1e090dc9b, ev-707cfb9a39bd]. Even so, nothing shown says which component owns the API, whether it's opt-in, or what happens to clusters whose operators do nothing. To write the subject, applicability and consequence aspects we need the RFC-0012 text, the PR description, or an upgrade-guide or docs section about ExternalArtifact.",
